{
  "id": "interleaving-string",
  "questionId": "interleaving-string",
  "slug": "interleaving-string",
  "title": "Interleaving String",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "strings"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "if s1 has length m and s2 has length n, and s3 doesn't have length m + n, you can return false immediately without any DP",
    "define dp[i][j] as true if the first i characters of s1 and the first j characters of s2 can interleave to form the first i + j characters of s3",
    "dp[i][j] is true if EITHER the last character came from s1 (s1[i-1] == s3[i+j-1] and dp[i-1][j] is true) OR it came from s2 (s2[j-1] == s3[i+j-1] and dp[i][j-1] is true)",
    "base case dp[0][0] = true (two empty strings interleave to an empty string); dp[i][0] and dp[0][j] are prefix checks against just s1 or just s2 respectively",
    "fill the table and return dp[m][n]"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "not checking the length of s3 upfront (m + n must equal s3.length or the answer is trivially false)",
    "indexing s3 incorrectly - the character being matched at dp[i][j] is s3[i+j-1], not s3[i-1] or s3[j-1] alone",
    "using OR when the recurrence needs both branches checked (from s1 or from s2), missing one and getting false negatives"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given three strings `s1`, `s2`, and `s3`. An interleaving means\n`s3` is built by repeatedly taking the next unused character from\neither `s1` or `s2` (never both at once), preserving the relative order\nof characters within each source string, until both are fully consumed.\n\n**Determine whether `s3` can be formed by interleaving `s1` and\n`s2`.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= s1.length, s2.length <= 100",
      "0 <= s3.length <= 200",
      "strings consist of lowercase English letters"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "s1 and s2 are both empty (s3 must also be empty)",
      "s3's length doesn't equal s1.length + s2.length (immediately false)",
      "one of s1 or s2 is empty (s3 must exactly equal the other one)",
      "s1 and s2 share overlapping characters, creating multiple possible interleavings to check"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s1 = \"aabcc\", s2 = \"dbbca\", s3 = \"aadbbcbcac\"",
        "output": "true",
        "expectedOutput": "true",
        "explanation": "One valid interleaving: aa (from s1) + dbbc (from s2) + bc (from s1) + a (from s2) + c (from s1)."
      },
      {
